  "notes": {
    "zone": "Zone 5 (the Bone Hollow, the beta dungeon, docs/specs/origins/dungeon-scope-beta.md): a zone with a roof, rows only. `level` is the zone number = its base level (Dom 2026-10-08). Default theme: the bone-and-skull cave camp (zone 90's look and the goblin-camp props kit), dark by data; Dom swaps the look through rows.",
    "spawns": "Existing creature rows only, copied from Zone 1 at this zone's band: cinder-scavenger (the goblin kin, Gobelinus) as the population, pit-goblin as the patrol, giant-salamander as the end fight with the troll treatment (a named row: zone level + the named lift, so hp x2 and +20% damage from the stage rows, as the cave troll).",
    "place": "The zone is MOUNTED in the shared world frame at the far end of the Drowned Marsh (the `hollow` join), more than presence's 40 m sight radius from every other zone, so nobody sees across zones and presence needs no change (Backend 2026-10-17); it is listed, so presence's walkable accepts it. The way in is not a link: the cave-mouth landmark is in Zone 1's own row (cinder-fields, beside the ash-pits camp) and the crossing is two exit rows (origins/zones/exit-rows.json, cave-mouth and hollow-gate): a door from one zone page to the other, with presence warp rows zone5-gate and zone1-cave-mouth. The fixed end-room ground piece is a ground-loot row at hollow-cache (outside the salamander's aggro).",
    "kit": "Zone 5's kit: a copy of Zone 2's until Characters ship this zone's own (the kit's node names are a contract)."
  }
